ent length |\n| $avgdl$ | Average document length |\n| $k_1$ | Controls term frequency saturation |\n| $b$ | Controls document length normalization |\n\nTypical values are:\n\n- $k_1 = 1.2$ to $2.0$\n- $b = 0.75$\n\n### Why BM25 is better than basic TF IDF\n\nImagine two documents:\n\n- D1: `Vector database` (2 words)\n- D2: `Vector database` repeated 50 times in a long document.\n\nA basic term frequency approach might give D2 an excessively high score because the query terms appear many times.\n\nBM25 uses term frequency saturation, meaning that repeating a term 50 times does not necessarily make the document 50 times more relevant.\n\nIt also normalizes for document length, helping avoid unfairly favoring longer documents.\n\nIn vector databases: BM25 is particularly useful for retrieving documents that contain exact keywords, technical terms, product names, identifiers, or specific phrases.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"pip install rank-bm25","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-02T13:00:47.35844Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-02T13:00:47.358942Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-02T13:00:49.901737Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-02T13:00:47.358897Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-02T13:00:49.900092Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Requirement already satisfied: rank-bm25 in /usr/local/lib/python3.13/dist-packages (0.2.2)\nRequirement already satisfied: numpy in /usr/local/lib/python3.13/dist-packages (from rank-bm25) (2.1.3)\nNote: you may need to restart the kernel to use updated packages.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":129},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from rank_bm25 import BM25Okapi\n\nquery = \"Machine Learning\"\n\n# Step 1: Tokenize documents\ntokenized_documents = [\n    doc.lower().split()\n    for doc in sentences1\n]\ntokenized_documents","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-02T13:00:49.903847Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-02T13:00:49.90440